---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import refs from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-12/references.json';
import v from '../../../../../public/equipment/15-12/verification.json';
const a='/equipment/15-12/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="TDT RZ6 and RA4PA · Documentary cases and offline trace reader" subtitle="" description="Inspect disconnected Tucker-Davis electronics and analyze peak timing in a fixed fictitious computer file." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment rz1512">
<nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/15-12/">← Equipment 15-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#evidence">Sources &amp; checks</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">15-12 / RZ6-A-P1 + four-channel RA4PA Medusa</span><h2>Tucker-Davis RZ6 &amp; Medusa · Offline peak timing</h2><p>Inspect two disconnected, unpowered electronics cases. In the separate reader, compare four fixed synthetic records and find the first whose peak meets an offline threshold. The records were not acquired from equipment or a biological source.</p></header>
<div class="dn-grid"><section class="dn-card"><h3>3D documentary exhibit</h3>
<div class="dn-bar"><button data-view="whole">Whole exhibit</button><button data-view="front">Rack front</button><button data-view="medusa">Medusa case</button><button data-view="chart">Offline reader</button><button id="camera-reset">Reset view</button></div>
<div class="dn-camera"><canvas id="rz-model" aria-label="Disconnected RZ6 rack face, small RA4PA Medusa case, and separately supported offline plot"></canvas></div>
<p id="asset" class="dn-note" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="dn-note">Drag to orbit, pinch or scroll to zoom. On the independent reader, the amber key analyzes the fixed file and the pale key cycles offline thresholds. The electronics cases have no actions.</p></section>
<section class="dn-card"><h3>Read the fixed trace file</h3><div class="dn-bar"><label>Offline threshold <select id="threshold"><option value="3">3 mV</option><option value="5" selected>5 mV</option><option value="6">6 mV</option><option value="7">7 mV</option><option value="9">9 mV</option></select></label><label>Preview clip <select id="clip"><option value="L1">L1</option><option value="L2">L2</option><option value="L3" selected>L3</option><option value="L4">L4</option></select></label></div>
<div class="dn-bar"><button class="primary" id="analyze">Analyze fixed file</button><button id="reset">Reset</button></div>
<canvas id="curve" width="486" height="276" role="img" aria-label="Synthetic voltage record against fixed time base, highlighted offline selection window and optional peak marker"></canvas>
<p class="dn-note" id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready: four authored records, 5 mV offline criterion, samples 62–102 only.</p>
<table id="summary" aria-label="Offline peak analysis by fixed record"><thead><tr><th>Record</th><th>Window peak</th><th>Qualifies</th><th>Offset</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td colspan="4">Analyze the fixed file to compare records.</td></tr></tbody></table>
<div class="dn-bar"><button id="json" disabled>Export result JSON</button><button id="csv" disabled>Export data CSV</button><a href={a+'example-result.json'}>Example result</a></div>
<p class="dn-note">The read-only rule checks samples 62–102 and accepts a window maximum at or above the chosen threshold. Earlier samples may be large but are outside the window. Offset is (peak index − 32) × 0.05 ms; a tie uses the earlier index. These numbers are not device settings, a sound stimulus, or biological thresholds.</p></section></div>
<section id="evidence"><h3>Source evidence and independent checks</h3>
<div class="photo-pair">
<figure><img src={a+'reference-front.webp'} width="640" height="400" alt="Original RZ6 rack face with blank display, sealed decorative faces and separate small preamp" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original render of the GLB. The <a href={refs.references[0].url}>TDT processor photograph</a> identifies the two front panel regions, dark status window and nominal rack face.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><img src={a+'reference-medusa.webp'} width="640" height="400" alt="Original isolated RA4PA enclosure with four unlit indicator marks" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Original close-up of the separate RA4PA exterior, based on the four-indicator vendor silhouette. Its size is estimated.</figcaption></figure>
</div>
<ul>{refs.references.map(r=><li><a href={r.url}>{r.title}</a>. {r.caption}</li>)}</ul>
<p>The chosen visual pairing is the RZ6-A-P1 and four-channel RA4PA, not the RA16PA or Medusa4Z. The documented front is <b>482.6 × 133.35 mm</b> (19 in × 3U). Body depth, rear details and RA4PA envelope are photo estimates. All surfaces are fixed and capped. No cables, headstage, acquisition, emitted audio, stimulation, hardware controls or biological handling are implemented.</p>
<div class="dn-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Tolerance</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody>{v.checks.map(c=><tr><th scope="row">{c.id}</th><td>{String(c.expected)} {c.unit}</td><td>{typeof c.actual==='number'?Number(c.actual.toFixed(8)):String(c.actual)} {c.unit}</td><td>{c.tolerance===0?'Exact':c.tolerance}</td><td>{c.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'build-model.py'} download>Editable 3D source</a> · <a href={a+'rz6-ra4pa-exteriors.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'references.json'}>Reference notes</a> · <a href={a+'vr-station.json'}>VR action manifest</a> · <a href={a+'offline.mjs'}>Independent analysis module</a> · <a href={a+'example-samples.csv'}>Example CSV</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification JSON</a>. No headset session tested.</p>
</section></article></Layout><script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/15-12/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
.rz1512{--dn-rule:color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 26%,transparent);max-width:1280px;margin:auto}.dn-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.08fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}.dn-card{min-width:0;border:1px solid var(--dn-rule);padding:.85rem;margin:.8rem 0}.dn-card h3{margin:.21rem 0 .6rem}.dn-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.45rem;margin:.53rem 0}.dn-bar,.dn-note,.dn-fig figcaption{font:.89rem/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif}
.rz1512 :is(button,select){font:inherit;padding:.4rem;background:var(--panel,Canvas);color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--dn-rule);border-radius:3px;min-height:38px;cursor:pointer}.rz1512 .primary{background:#34594f;color:#fff}.dn-camera{aspect-ratio:1.34;background:#263b40}.dn-camera canvas{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;touch-action:none}.rz1512 #curve{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:492px;margin:.6rem 0}.dn-table{overflow:auto}.dn-table table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse}.dn-table :is(td,th){border-bottom:1px solid var(--dn-rule);padding:.42rem;text-align:left}.dn-fig{margin:1rem 0;max-width:680px}.dn-fig img{width:100%;height:auto;display:block}.dn-fig figcaption{margin:.38rem 0}@media(max-width:850px){.dn-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
.rz1512 .photo-pair{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.8rem;max-width:860px}.rz1512 .photo-pair figure{margin:0}.rz1512 .photo-pair img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}.rz1512 .photo-pair figcaption{font:.86rem/1.4 system-ui,sans-serif;margin:.3rem 0}@media(max-width:600px){.rz1512 .photo-pair{grid-template-columns:1fr}}.rz1512 button:disabled{opacity:.55;cursor:default}.rz1512 #summary{font:.86rem/1.35 system-ui,sans-serif;width:100%;text-align:left}.rz1512 #summary :is(td,th){padding:.28rem .25rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--dn-rule)}</style>
